  "dependencies_note": "Each zip is placed and unpacked at dist/<name>-<version>/<name>.zip before the build, where the recipe looks for it, so the recipe never downloads. The URLs are the recipe's own except FFmpeg, which is the 1.0.0 release asset. Hashes were taken on 2026-09-25; FFmpeg and reference match the values recorded in IOS-POC-17I.",
  "reference": {
    "name": "Libmpv.xcframework.zip",
    "url": "https://github.com/mpvkit/MPVKit/releases/download/1.0.0/Libmpv.xcframework.zip",
    "bytes": 19184048,
    "sha256": "c381ceb4c1504efac12da95293e56585bbeb691634aa64e3a729f517169933ba",
    "note": "The upstream artifact the app used until IOS-POC-17I. The workflow requires the ios-arm64 slice of the new build to match it in libmpv's Configuration and enabled-features strings, archive members, defined external symbols and framework files; undefined symbols may differ only through the context_moltenvk member, plus one named toolchain exception: _wcslen, used only by filters_f_hwtransfer.c.o, where Xcode 26's clang turns the loop counting the zero-terminated supported_formats list into wcslen (the same loop on Apple platforms, where wchar_t is a 32-bit int). The user accepted that exception on 2026-09-25 after run 36085068570."
  },
  "toolchain": {
    "runner": "macos-26",
